# --- Disk-encryption posture ------------------------------------------------
#
# Same knob name as the Core hop installer so a Double VPN deploy can set one
# value for both roles. A LUKS root is no longer mandatory. Full-disk
# encryption on Ubuntu 24.04 must be chosen at install time; there is no
# supported in-place conversion, so this is a choice between two postures:
#
#   luks       Require a LUKS-backed root. Strongest.
#   substitute Do not require LUKS. Require the SUBSTITUTE CONTROL SET instead
#              (see verify_disk_encryption_posture) and refuse if it cannot be
#              established.
#   auto       (default) Use "luks" when the root is already LUKS-backed,
#              otherwise "substitute".
#
# There is deliberately NO "none"/"off"/"skip" value. REQUIRE_LUKS_ROOT=1 is
# retained as an alias that forces "luks"; it conflicts with an explicit
# CORE_DISK_ENCRYPTION_MODE=substitute and that conflict is a refusal.
#
# THE HONEST DIFFERENCE: the substitute set protects secrets from a
# RUNNING-HOST adversary. It does NOT protect a POWERED-OFF DISK that is
# physically removed, imaged, or seized, nor a cold provider-side snapshot
# of the block device. That single case is what LUKS buys.
CORE_DISK_ENCRYPTION_MODE="${CORE_DISK_ENCRYPTION_MODE:-auto}"
CORE_DISK_ENCRYPTION_EFFECTIVE=""
NODE_FAIL2BAN_IGNOREIPS_DEFAULT="${NODE_FAIL2BAN_IGNOREIPS:-127.0.0.1/8 ::1}"
